  "caption": "Quinn's knee X-ray said \"bone on bone\", so Quinn decided to stop moving. Weeks later, the knee felt even stiffer.\n\nX-rays show the space between bones, not how a joint feels. Imaging and pain often don't match, and pain also depends on muscle strength, sleep, stress and mood. Avoiding movement can lead to weaker muscles and stiffer joints.\n\nWhat often helps: exercise is a first-line treatment for knee and hip arthritis at every X-ray grade, research hasn't shown it speeds up cartilage loss, and a three-month plan to build strength can make a real difference to how you move.\n\nIf pain or stiffness keeps limiting your day, get it checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
